			"notes": "BBS Renewed 2.5.0 preview for **Minecraft 26.3 / Fabric**.\n\nDownload **`bbs-2.5.0-26.3.jar`** and put it in `mods` together with Fabric API for 26.3.\nRequires **Java 25** and **Fabric Loader 0.19.5 or newer**.\n\nPreview 2 corrects the GPL v2 copies included in Preview 1: the final paragraph of\nthe application appendix was missing. Both bundled copies now contain the complete,\nunmodified text from GNU GCC. Comparing every decompressed JAR entry confirms that\n**only those two licence files changed**. Every program class and all other resources\nare byte-identical to Preview 1.\n\nThis contains the integrated 26.3 product: updated film and animation tools, Regie\nworkspace, texture editor, independent held-prop hand bindings, and Blender/Resolve\nintegrations. The first-launch category-settings error is fixed.\n\nPreview 1's frozen product passed Windows/Linux world and dashboard tests, plus\nOpenGL and two Vulkan launches on Linux/NVIDIA. Its final\n[Windows/Linux CI run](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/actions/runs/38971400388)\nis green. Preview 2 passes the build, Blender provenance and product/private-companion\nboundary checks. The licence-only rebuild is not a new gameplay acceptance run.\n\nThis remains a **preview**. Full rig/shader/long-session and cross-editor parity are\nnot established by the smoke tests. A preliminary development-selector Vulkan run\nhit a semaphore timeout whose cause remains unestablished; both final frozen-product\nVulkan runs passed. See the [release record](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/blob/8d1520dfc4a86f9258e8b4f3bb7e7519994296de/docs/RELEASE-26.3.md).\n\nThe complete buildable source is `bbs-renewed-2.5.0-26.3-source.zip`; `sources.jar`\nis provided separately. `SHA256SUMS.txt` covers all three archives. Original copyright,\nMIT, Blender GPL and other third-party notices are retained. The private development\ncompanion is not needed to use this release.\n\nThe older Minecraft versions are being ported and checked against the same feature\nsnapshot. This release targets **26.3**.\n\nVerification record update, 2026-10-17: the old server GameTest task contained no server test functions and supplies no assertion evidence. The Windows/Linux world/dashboard evidence comes from the actual client runs. The [public solver record](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/blob/8d1520dfc4a86f9258e8b4f3bb7e7519994296de/docs/BLENDER-IK-PROVENANCE-2026-10-15.md), also attached separately, replaces the missing internal documentation links in the frozen source export. The actual anonymous product JAR passes all 22 numerical reference cases at 1e-6, with maximum difference 2.90000001e-8. This is solver-component evidence; broader rig/editor/recording acceptance remains separate. The original binary and source archives retain their published hashes."
		},
