			"notes": "Superseded by [Preview 2](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/releases/tag/v2.5.0-26.3-rc.2), which supplies the complete GPL v2 text. Preview 1 omitted the final paragraph of the application appendix. Program classes and all other product resources are byte-identical.\n\nBBS Renewed 2.5.0 preview for **Minecraft 26.3 / Fabric**.\n\nDownload **`bbs-2.5.0-26.3.jar`** and put it in `mods` together with Fabric API for 26.3.\nRequires **Java 25** and **Fabric Loader 0.19.5 or newer**.\n\nThis packages the current integrated 26.3 product: updated film and animation tools,\nRegie workspace, texture editor, independent held-prop hand bindings, and the Blender/Resolve\nintegrations. The first-launch category-settings error is fixed.\n\nVerified: production world/dashboard tests on Windows and Linux, plus OpenGL and two Vulkan\nlaunches on the same frozen Linux/NVIDIA product JAR. The final\n[Windows/Linux CI run](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/actions/runs/38971400388)\nis green. The product/private-companion boundary and Blender source-provenance gate pass.\n\nThis is a **preview**, with the tested scope and remaining limitations in the\n[release record](https://github.com/AfrobamaYT/BBS-Renewed-/blob/v2.5.0-26.3-rc.1/docs/RELEASE-26.3.md).\nA preliminary development-selector Vulkan run hit a semaphore timeout; its cause is not\nestablished. Both final frozen-product Vulkan runs passed. Full rig/shader/long-session and\ncross-editor parity are not established by these smoke tests.\n\nThe complete buildable source is `bbs-renewed-2.5.0-26.3-source.zip`. The `sources.jar` is\nprovided separately. `SHA256SUMS` covers all three archives. Original copyright, MIT,\nBlender GPL and other third-party notices are retained. The private development companion\nis not needed to use this release.\n\nThe other Minecraft versions will receive the same feature snapshot through separate ports\nand runtime checks; this release is for **26.3**."
		}
